// items.js — the magic items of SRD 5.2.1 (CC BY 4.0), one line each. Names and
// rarities are checked against the SRD text; Potion of Poison has no type line
// in the text we checked, so its rarity is the one from the earlier SRD. The
// notes are our own short summaries for the table: they say what the item is
// for, and the book is still the place for the exact rules. Artifacts are left
// out on purpose.
//
// th   — the hoard theme the item suits best: arcane | martial | trade | relic
// att  — needs attunement: 1, or { ru, en } naming who can attune
// use  — used up when used (potions, scrolls, dusts); priced at half
// bad  — cursed or a trap: the GM should know before handing it over
// pick — a set of VARIANTS to roll for this item
